//   2. With STCE=1, every CSR instruction form on stimecmp in S-mode (csrrw with rd=x0 and rd!=x0,
//     csrrs/csrrc with rs1=x0 and rs1!=x0, csrrwi, csrrsi with uimm=0, csrrci) returns the old
//     value and leaves the value the form defines; on RV32 also on stimecmph.
//   3. With STCE=1 the comparison drives sip.STIP: stimecmp=0 gives STIP=1, all ones gives 0.
//   4. Enabling is for S-mode only: with STCE=1 and TM=1, U-mode reads and writes still raise
//     illegal-instruction, with scounteren.TM at 1 and 0 (a counter enable must not leak to
//     stimecmp).
